From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shell32: BindToStorage, GetDetailsEx and Initialize of the virtual folders (3701)

shell32: BindToStorage, GetDetailsEx and Initialize of the virtual folders

The desktop, This PC, Control Panel and Network folders had BindToStorage
and GetDetailsEx stubs and refused IPersistFolder::Initialize, and the file
system folder had no GetDetailsEx.

BindToStorage of an item that is a file gives the file's stream, as the file
system folder does; anything else fails, with E_NOINTERFACE for an interface
that is no stream. GetDetailsEx gives what the item has by itself first (a
file's size as a 64-bit integer, its dates as variant dates, its names), and
else the text of the folder's column for that property. Initialize stores
the place a folder object is given (This PC, Control Panel, Network); the
desktop is the root and one object serves everyone, so it takes its own
place only. The Network folder now parses a computer by its bare name.
